  <metadata>
    <name>S04 The forgotten north coast</name>
    <desc>Section 04 of the Flores Race traverse: Where the water and the track both run out. 156.6 km, +2335 m / -2868 m, starts at km 371 of the course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:57Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.530820" lon="120.443500">
    <ele>559.6</ele>
    <name>Liang Bua</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- The village and limestone cave ~14 km NW of Ruteng where Homo floresiensis was found (2003). Small vendor stalls at the site; no lodging confirmed.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.309600" lon="120.490780">
    <ele>11.1</ele>
    <name>Reo</name>
    <desc>km 54.4 | kind: port | resupply: basic | water: reliable | sleep: homestay -- Old north-coast port town in Reok kecamatan: market, bank, gas station, health centre, mosque and church, a homestay (Reo Family Homestay). The port facility itself sits a few km west at the Wae Reo river mouth (see the </desc>
    <sym>Anchor</sym>
    <type>anchor/port</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.347490" lon="120.757860">
    <ele>12.2</ele>
    <name>Pota</name>
    <desc>km 106.3 | kind: port | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- North-coast village/port in Sambi Rampas kecamatan, Manggarai Timur: parish church, health centre, bank unit, schools. End of the west region's corridor; onward to Riung is the next agent's territory.</desc>
    <sym>Anchor</sym>
    <type>anchor/port</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.419000" lon="121.029000">
    <ele>22.4</ele>
    <name>Riung</name>
    <desc>km 156.6 | kind: port | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: guesthouse -- Fishing port and gateway village for the Seventeen Islands marine park; small shops and a market, several homestays/losmen serving divers and boat tourists. Coordinates hand-placed from the Riung Nature Reserve boundary </desc>
    <sym>Anchor</sym>
    <type>anchor/port</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.530820" lon="120.443500">
    <ele>559.6</ele>
    <name>Liang Bua</name>
    <desc>[anchor] Limestone cave ~14 km NW of Ruteng where the remains of Homo floresiensis ("the hobbit") were excavated in 2003 -- the deep-time hook of the whole race.</desc>
    <sym>Tunnel</sym>
    <type>poi/cave</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.286050" lon="120.453310">
    <ele>11.2</ele>
    <name>Reo port</name>
    <desc>[resupply] The working port at the Wae Reo river mouth on the north coast, handling inter-island cargo and ferries; a candidate second export port for the region (Pelabuhan Kedindi).</desc>
    <sym>Anchor</sym>
    <type>poi/port</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.420800" lon="121.027500">
    <ele>20.9</ele>
    <name>Seventeen Islands Marine Park</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] A marine park of more than twenty coral islets off Riung's north coast, reached by hired boat from the Riung pier; snorkelling, white-sand islets, flying foxes on Pulau Tembang.</desc>
    <sym>Park</sym>
    <type>poi/national-park</type>
  </wpt>
